+{ ports/dos speed patch (scan-targets): the same scan in the built-in assembler. The table, the order of the pairs
+  (K then J), the strict "fewer steps" test, the stored Head, Key and Val and the final SortTable are the Pascal's;
+  FootprintCell is read inline (Footprints[Kind, Index], valid when DX >= 0, as in ovl31). Two shortcuts that
+  change no result:
+  - with Dir 8 or $FF (every caller passes $FF) InDirArc is True exactly when both points are on the map (X 0..49,
+    Y 0..24), so that test is inline (once per candidate and per target cell); any other Dir calls InDirArc;
+  - WalkLine is not called when it must fail on its step limit: its line's First grows by 2 or 3 a step and ends at
+    2 * max(|DX|, |DY|) + min(|DX|, |DY|) on the end point (checked for every displacement on the 50 by 25 map),
+    and the walk fails once First > 2 * MaxSteps + 1. WalkLine changes nothing outside its own var parameters,
+    which are locals here. A range-1 scan (the AI's adjacent-enemy test) now walks only the neighbours.
+  The working direction of a hit (Dir 8 or $FF) is InDirArc's first True direction from 0, worked out from the
+  displacement (below); another Dir of 8 or more still calls InDirArc with 0, 1, ... }
